  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186119784,
      "id": "e69a4aee-6e92-598b-99b5-1d830b6dea54",
      "title": "Identifying Correct Statements About a Matrix"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 7 & 0 \\\\ -7 & -7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- $A$ is upper triangular: **false**. The entry in row 2, column 1 is $-7\\ne 0$, below the main diagonal.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 7 & 0 \\\\ -7 & -7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $A$ is lower triangular: **false**. The entry in row 1, column 2 is $7\\ne 0$, above the main diagonal.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 7 & 0 \\\\ -7 & -7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $A+{A}^{T}$ is upper triangular: **true**. All entries below the main diagonal are zero.\n\n$$\nA+{A}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}16 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -14 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
      ":question/id": "2348a805-98d1-5902-972c-24cd79a49920",
