      "id": "e69a4aee-6e92-598b-99b5-1d830b6dea54",
      "title": "Identifying Correct Statements About a Matrix"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- $A$ is lower triangular: **true**. All entries above the main diagonal are zero.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- ${A}^{T}-A$ is lower triangular: **false**. The entry in row 2, column 3 is $2\\ne 0$, above the main diagonal.\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}-A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $A$ is upper triangular: **false**. The entry in row 3, column 2 is $2\\ne 0$, below the main diagonal.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
      ":question/id": "95225f54-c17c-537f-8940-15f543e384fc",
