      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- $A$ is upper triangular: **false**. The entry in row 3, column 2 is $5\\ne 0$, below the main diagonal.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $A^{T} + A$ is upper triangular: **true**. All entries below the main diagonal are zero.\n\n$$\nA^{T} + A=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 12 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $A$ is lower triangular: **false**. The entry in row 2, column 3 is $-5\\ne 0$, above the main diagonal.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
