    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & -4 & -7 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 0 & 8\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- $A$ is upper triangular: **false**. The entry in row 2, column 1 is $4\\ne 0$, below the main diagonal.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & -4 & -7 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 0 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $A^{T} + A$ is upper triangular: **true**. All entries below the main diagonal are zero.\n\n$$\nA^{T} + A=\\begin{bmatrix}-14 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 16\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $A$ is lower triangular: **false**. The entry in row 1, column 2 is $-4\\ne 0$, above the main diagonal.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & -4 & -7 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 0 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
